::U6F2_01::Alcohol is a {=central-nervous-system depressant ~vitamin ~antibiotic ~stimulant only}

::U6F2_02::A U.S. standard drink contains about {=14 grams of pure alcohol ~14 grams of sugar ~one container of any size ~zero ethanol}

::U6F2_03::BAC means {=blood alcohol concentration ~a personal safe limit ~beverage alcohol color ~breathing alert code}

::U6F2_04::Coffee or a cold shower {=does not quickly remove alcohol; time is required ~guarantees sobriety ~lowers BAC to zero ~prevents impairment}

::U6F2_05::Impaired driving risk involves {=reduced judgment, reaction time, coordination, and attention ~only beverage taste ~only road knowledge ~no brain functions}

::U6F2_06::Alcohol-overdose signs include {=unresponsiveness and abnormal breathing ~better coordination ~mild thirst only ~faster speech only}

::U6F2_07::Underage abstinence {=avoids developmental, legal, safety, and goal risks ~guarantees popularity ~replaces help-seeking ~makes driving safer after use}

::U6F2_08::Suspected alcohol overdose requires {=emergency services, monitoring, directions, and staying ~sleeping alone ~coffee ~walking}
